<!-- FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1 F6 build ("The boughway network — elevated
     lanes"). fever_wood_kit_spec.md F6: "lanes are RUT_Boughway TerrainDef
     — low pathCost, raised sprite, affordance Medium (INVENTED affordance
     tier per §7b: platforms yes, bunkers no — heavy goes on F5's stilts or
     in F7's bore-caves)". Painted entirely by RM_GenStep_RootCauseways
     (RUT_FeverWood.xml's own RM_RootCausewayBiomeExtension, primary
     profile) — not buildable, not in any construction designation
     category, same posture RUT_RootCauseway's own header already
     established for the sibling kit's ground lane.

     RESOLVED ❓ (the spec's own "verify the donor's water terrains accept
     a Bridgeable-style replacement, or route lanes around pools at gen
     time"): checked against the real 1.6/Odyssey decompile this pass,
     Verse/TerrainGrid.cs:193 TerrainGrid.SetTerrain — the method GenStep
     map-painting actually calls has NO terrainAffordanceNeeded/Bridgeable
     check at all (only null/bounds/temporary/isFoundation branches); that
     gating only exists on the PLAYER-CONSTRUCTION path
     (BuildableDef.terrainAffordanceNeeded + GenConstruct.cs:494, F5's own
     engine route), which map-gen terrain painting never goes through. So
     there is no real "Bridgeable-style replacement" mechanism to reuse in
     the first place — the simpler and more honest route, taken here, is
     to never paint a boughway cell over a registered pool at all: the
     RM_RootCausewayBiomeExtension wired onto RUT_FeverWood sets
     basinTerrains to the biome's own two buildable ground terrains
     (Soil/SoilRich, RUT_FeverWood.xml's own terrainsByFertility list) as
     an ALLOWLIST — RM_GenStep_RootCauseways.PaintFootprint's existing
     "restricted to basinTerrains" check (built for Greentide's opposite
     use, painting ONLY over its churnmud basin) doubles as an EXCLUDE of
     everything not in that list, including RUT_FeverWoodMirrorPool and
     RUT_StiltPlatform, with zero new C#. This preserves F1's pool-terrain
     registry (RUT_MapComponent_TheTenant's own terrain-grid scan would
     lose a cell if a boughway simply overwrote it) and the lore's own
     "nothing goes in the water here" — genuinely simpler than inventing a
     drawn-fiction bridge visual with no engine mechanism behind it.

     pathCost 1 (lower than RUT_RootCauseway's 2 — "fast... lanes" per the
     spec's own player-experience text). affordances Light+Medium only, no
     Heavy — "platforms yes, bunkers no" (INVENTED tier, per the spec's own
     citation).

     ART: reuses vanilla WoodPlankFloor's own texture path unmodified
     (confirmed real, Data/Core/Defs/TerrainDefs/Terrain_Floors.xml,
     texturePath Terrain/Surfaces/WoodFloor) — the same texture
     RUT_StiltPlatform already reuses via its own Bridge ancestry, tinted
     here to read as living wood rather than milled planking. Terrain
     texture reuse is not the "Things/" namespace-ownership check
     validate_patch.py enforces for ThingDefs in this mod (RUT_RootCauseway/
     RUT_StiltPlatform's own headers already establish this for terrain),
     so no placeholder PNG or DEPLOY_HOLD entry is needed. Real bespoke
     raised-lane art is still owed to the standing art pipeline, same
     disclosure as RUT_StiltPlatform's own. -->
<Defs>

  <TerrainDef>
    <defName>RUT_Boughway</defName>
    <label>boughway</label>
    <description>A living lane grown across the crown — bark and root woven flat and firm well above the black pools below. Fast, safe, and never quite where the map says it was last season.</description>
    <renderPrecedence>326</renderPrecedence>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WoodFloor</texturePath>
    <pathCost>1</pathCost>
    <fertility>0</fertility>
    <edgeType>FadeRough</edgeType>
    <color>(87,66,38)</color>
    <affordances>
      <li>Light</li>
      <li>Medium</li>
    </affordances>
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>1</Beauty>
    </statBases>
  </TerrainDef>

</Defs>
